; ascii.tal - printable ASCII from the 512_8 font, as data.
; GENERATED, do not edit by hand; it comes from tools/font512.py, which
; reads the upstream .txt for the bitmaps and the .tab for the names.
;
; The space, the letters, the digits and the punctuation: $20 to $7e,
; ninety five glyphs, 760 bytes. It comes out of a 512 glyph font, which
; is 4096 bytes, and replaced a hand-built 41 glyph table of 328 bytes.
; The full set is not wanted: nothing on this machine draws anything else,
; and the machine has 32256 bytes of code and data to spend, which is
; plenty but not unlimited.
;
; From https://github.com/alexfru/512_8, sans, which upstream calls thin with poor contrast. At 8x8 that is not subtle: the colon is two single pixels and the full stop is one. Upstream recommends bold instead.
; Public domain, Unlicense: nothing is owed for using it and nothing has
; to be credited. Upstream ships bold, sans and serif; they carry the same
; characters at the same indices and differ only in the shapes, so the
; style is chosen by which upstream file tools/font512.py was pointed at.
;
; THE INDEX IS THE CHARACTER, MINUS THE SPACE
; ----------------------------------------
; The glyph for character code c is at @font + (c - $20) * 8, so glyph
; zero is the space and the digits are $10 to $19 and A to Z are $21 to
; $2a. That is the reason this range was chosen contiguous: a character
; is one subtraction away from its own offset, with no table of mappings
; and no search. The 512 glyph font cannot do this, because its index is
; not its code point below $28 and not above $7e at all - glyph 1 is a
; smiling face - which is why a subset like this one is the thing to use
; rather than the whole table.
;
; 8 wide, 8 down, one byte a row, bit 7 the leftmost pixel: the layout
; @glyph in fontlib.tal already expects, so these bytes are used exactly
; as upstream has them and nothing is converted.

@font
        DB $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00        ; $20  U+00A0, blank
        DB $00, $10, $10, $10, $10, $00, $10, $00        ; $21  U+203C
        DB $00, $44, $44, $28, $00, $00, $00, $00        ; $22  upstream unlisted
        DB $00, $48, $fc, $48, $48, $fc, $48, $00        ; $23  upstream unlisted
        DB $10, $7c, $90, $7c, $12, $92, $7c, $10        ; $24  upstream unlisted
        DB $00, $44, $e8, $50, $28, $5c, $88, $00        ; $25  upstream unlisted
        DB $00, $20, $50, $64, $98, $88, $74, $00        ; $26  upstream unlisted
        DB $00, $10, $10, $20, $00, $00, $00, $00        ; $27  U+2019
        DB $00, $08, $10, $10, $10, $10, $08, $00        ; $28  U+0028  '('
        DB $00, $20, $10, $10, $10, $10, $20, $00        ; $29  U+0029  ')'
        DB $00, $00, $48, $30, $fc, $30, $48, $00        ; $2a  U+002A  '*'
        DB $00, $00, $10, $10, $7c, $10, $10, $00        ; $2b  U+002B  '+'
